# Project-scope mapping for GitHub Packages. Committed on purpose: the mapping
# itself is not a secret, and it is what stops an accidental `npm publish` from
# going to npmjs.org instead. Note the precedence: a `@scope:registry` mapping
# outranks `publishConfig.registry`, which is why the release workflow asserts
# the effective registry before it publishes.
#
# It is NOT enough on its own. GitHub Packages only accepts a personal access
# token (classic) with `write:packages` (plus `read:packages`, and
# `delete:packages` if you ever unpublish). The OAuth token `gh auth login`
# stores does not carry those scopes. Authenticate once per machine:
#
#   npm login --scope=@brucezhang1993 --auth-type=legacy \
#     --registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
#   # Username: BruceZhang1993
#   # Password: <classic PAT with write:packages>
#
# `npm login` writes the token to your user-level ~/.npmrc
# (`//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=…`), so no credential ever lands in this
# repository. In GitHub Actions, `actions/setup-node` writes that same line from
# NODE_AUTH_TOKEN, which is why no token lives here.
@brucezhang1993:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
